            <tr><td class="band"><a href="/knowledge-center/">Knowledge Center</a></td><td>Free AI assessments with instant scoring</td><td>SMB AI Readiness Score, AI Knowledge Test</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="band"><a href="/playbooks/">Playbooks</a></td><td>Plain-English guides, like this one</td><td>AI readiness and AI literacy guides</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <div class="cav">The extras</div>
        <h2 id="utilities">What standalone tools does Best Answer Hub include?</h2>
        <p>Beyond the themed hubs, the main <a href="/tools/">Tools hub</a> holds a set of standalone generators and utilities that do not belong to a single category. They handle the quick, one-off jobs: making a QR code or a strong password, checking a site's speed or broken links, compressing an image, or running a focus session. Each one runs in your browser with no account and no upload, exactly like the tools in the themed hubs. The three groups below link straight to every standalone tool.</p>
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Tools</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="band">Generators</td><td><a href="/tools/qr-code-generator/">QR Code</a>, <a href="/tools/password-generator/">Password</a>, <a href="/tools/favicon-generator/">Favicon</a>, <a href="/tools/color-palette-generator/">Color Palette</a>, <a href="/tools/meta-tag-generator/">Meta Tag</a>, and <a href="/tools/citation-generator/">Citation</a></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="band">Site and SEO checkers</td><td><a href="/tools/website-speed-test/">Website Speed Test</a>, <a href="/tools/seo-score-checker/">SEO Score Checker</a>, <a href="/tools/broken-link-checker/">Broken Link Checker</a>, and <a href="/tools/ip-address-checker/">IP Address Checker</a></td></tr>
            <tr><td class="band">Everyday utilities</td><td><a href="/tools/pomodoro-timer/">Pomodoro Timer</a>, <a href="/tools/spin-wheel/">Spin Wheel</a>, <a href="/tools/image-compressor/">Image Compressor</a>, and <a href="/tools/screenshot-beautifier/">Screenshot Beautifier</a></td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>

        <div class="cav">Find your shelf</div>
        <h2 id="pick">How do I pick the right tool?</h2>
        <p>Start from the job, not the tool. Decide what you need to do, and the hub follows. If you are not sure, the search bar on the <a href="/tools/">Tools hub</a> finds any tool by name or keyword.</p>
